np("N001","n=λ+1>0 and |I|=n. For every integer t≥0, h y^t v=(λ−2t)y^t v; for t≥1, x y^t v=t(λ−t+1)y^(t−1)v. The vectors (e_i)_{i∈I} form a complex basis of V, and y^(λ+1)v=0 (hence all higher lowering powers vanish). On this basis, xe_0=0, xe_i=(λ−i+1)e_(i−1) for 1≤i≤λ, ye_i=(i+1)e_(i+1) for 0≤i<λ, ye_λ=0, he_i=(λ−2i)e_i. For all i∈I and natural r, X_r e_i=binom(λ−i+r,r)e_(i−r) if r≤i and zero otherwise; Y_r e_i=binom(i+r,r)e_(i+r) if i+r≤λ and zero otherwise. All displayed divided-power coefficients are integers.",["D001","D002","D003","D004","D006"],["n","λ","I","V","v","x","y","h","e","X","Y"],[par("t","nonnegative integer"),par("i","element of I"),par("r","natural number")],"problem.md:45-84"),
np("N002","iota embeds M_R as the R-span of M in V; M_R is free of rank n over R and its complex span is V. Each X_r and Y_r (r≥0) preserves M and M_R, and x,y,h preserve M and M_R. For every i,j∈I, E_ij preserves M_R (under iota). The following identities hold on V: Pi=Y_λ X_λ=E_λλ, X_(λ−i)Pi=E_iλ, Pi Y_(λ−j)=binom(λ,j)E_λj, and E_ij=binom(λ,j)^(-1) X_(λ−i)Pi Y_(λ−j), where binom(λ,j) is a unit in R.",["D001","D002","D003","D004","D006","D007","D008","D009","D010","D011"],["n","R","M","M_R","iota","V","X","Y","x","y","h","I","E","Pi","λ"],[par("r","natural number"),par("i","element of I"),par("j","element of I")],"problem.md:86-116; lattice-operator well-definedness from admissibility"),
np("N003","For every i∈I one has J_i=J. The R-module J⊂ℂ is nonzero and finitely generated. The map (c_i)_{i∈I}↦∑_{i∈I}c_i e_i is an R-linear isomorphism ∏_{i∈I}J→iota(M_R), so, identifying M_R through iota, M_R=⊕_{i∈I}J e_i.",["D002","D006","D007","D008","D009","D012","D013"],["I","J_i","J","R","e","iota","M_R"],[par("i","element of I"),par("c","I-indexed family of elements of J")],"problem.md:118-130"),
np("N004","The multiplication map ℚ⊗_R J→ℂ is injective and its image is the rational span of J, a one-dimensional ℚ-vector space. There exists b∈J with b≠0 and J=Rb. For any such b, the family (b e_i)_{i∈I} is an R-basis of M_R identified with iota(M_R).",["D002","D006","D007","D008","D009","D013"],["R","J","I","e","M_R","iota"],[par("b","complex number"),par("i","element of I")],"problem.md:132-148"),
np("N005","The natural tensor maps give K-linear isomorphisms V_K≅M_R⊗_R K≅(M_R/pM_R)⊗_(F_p)K, intertwining all lattice operators. There exists a K-basis (b_i)_{i∈I} of V_K obtained from an R-basis (b e_i) of M_R with b∈J nonzero. In particular dim_K(V_K)=n=λ+1>0. On this basis the induced operators satisfy xb_0=0, xb_i=(λ−i+1)b_(i−1) for 1≤i≤λ, yb_i=(i+1)b_(i+1) for i<λ, yb_λ=0, hb_i=(λ−2i)b_i, with integer coefficients interpreted in K. For every 0≤r≤λ, r! is nonzero in K and the induced divided powers X_r,Y_r equal (r!)^(-1)x^r,(r!)^(-1)y^r. Every binom(λ,j) for j∈I is nonzero in K. The reduced operators T_ij=binom(λ,j)^(-1) X_(λ−i)(Y_λ X_λ)Y_(λ−j), for i,j∈I, obey T_ij b_k=δ_jk b_i for every k∈I, where δ_jk is 1 for j=k and 0 otherwise.",["D001","D002","D003","D004","D006","D007","D008","D009","D013","D014","D016","D017"],["K","V_K","M_R","p","F_p","I","e","J","n","λ","x","y","h","X","Y","R","kappa","iota"],[par("b","complex number"),par("b_i","I-indexed family of vectors of V_K"),par("i","element of I"),par("j","element of I"),par("k","element of I"),par("r","integer"),par("T","I×I-indexed family of K-linear endomorphisms of V_K")],"problem.md:150-170"),
