{id:"R001",dependency_and_local_assumption_check:"H002 gives the finite index interval and n>0 at S001; H003 supplies both commutators and dim V=n, and H004 supplies the highest-weight equations and v≠0. S001 proves the full simultaneous induction, handling the t=0 x term separately and discharging L1. S002's nonzero factorial product grounds F002. S003's polynomial in h isolates every coefficient under L2, which is discharged before the basis conclusion F003. S004 compares the absent eigenvalue against that basis, so termination is derived, not assumed; S005's finite products and endpoint zeros give all divided powers.",source_application_check:"No E/M is used. Routine local linear algebra at S003 uses a linearly independent family with exactly dim V vectors, with size from H002/F001 and dimension from H003. The coefficient-isolation proof is displayed. S004's expansion uses F003 and nonzero complex eigenvalue differences. S005's integer binomial values have nonnegative integer arguments in the stated ranges; the falling/rising products are explicitly shown.",declaration_check:"D003–D004 distinguish enveloping elements from their actions; D006 introduces e without granting a basis. The induction t is scoped to S001; arbitrary coordinate i is live S002–S005, c,j only at S003, z only S004, and r only S005. Statement-local t0,i0 in F001,F002,F004 avoid local shadowing. All denominators are factorials in ℂ, and the basis guard needed by later E is proved here without using E."},
{id:"R002",dependency_and_local_assumption_check:"Direct N001 supplies the complex basis and all X,Y matrices. H005 provides a compatible integer/complex basis m and all divided-power lattice stability; H003 gives h=xy−yx, and H001–H002 give localization and prime bounds. S001 displays tensor coordinate maps to prove iota injective, freeness and span. S002 checks all input-index cases for Pi Y_(λ−j) and proves p∤binom(λ,j) through the factorial identity. S003 composes only preserving operators and a scalar in R. No extra lattice-normalization assumption or reduced-weight argument appears.",source_application_check:"No E/M is invoked. The basis extension in S001 is justified by extending the integer coordinate isomorphism and its inverse, not by an unsupported rank claim. S002 uses only the full exported divided-power identities in N001, prime arithmetic from H001–H002 and the definition of R. S003 checks E_iλ E_λj=E_ij on the available basis.",declaration_check:"The witness m is grounded in H005, with its n-element indexing justified by N001. Arbitrary i,j run over I and k is local to the basis evaluations. D007–D009 have H001, n and Pi have H002, and D010 has the direct N001 guard. The abstract tensor M_R is identified with its image only after injectivity is actually established at S001."},
{id:"R003",dependency_and_local_assumption_check:"S001 uses N002's preserving E_ij and N001's basis to prove each J_j⊆J_i and the reverse inclusion. S002 chooses coordinates of the arbitrary u using N001; N002 keeps every coordinate in M_R, and the converse sum inclusion plus independence establishes the full isomorphism F002. S003 projects n generators of M_R to generate J e_i, transports them through c↦c e_i, and proves J≠0 using the nonempty basis and complex span. No assumption that J⊂ℂ has rational rank one is made.",source_application_check:"No E/M is invoked. The only routine finite-generation fact is that the image of a module generated by n elements is generated by their n images, explicitly stated at S003. The transport J≅J e_i is injective because N001 says e_i≠0, and surjective by its displayed form. Every use of matrix units is supported by direct N002, not an ancestor proof body.",declaration_check:"The coordinate-module definitions D012–D013 use membership in iota(M_R); H001,H002 and the direct N001 guard for E are present. Arbitrary i,j,c and u have bounded scopes; d is a coordinate witness from N001 for iota(u). The revised F001 consistently binds i0 in J_i0, E_i0i0 and e_i0, so its exported local statement is actually universal."},
{id:"R004",dependency_and_local_assumption_check:"N003 supplies J finite, nonzero and the coordinate decomposition; N002 supplies free rank n; N001 supplies |I|=n>0 and independent e. S001 proves finite dimension of QJ and injectivity into ℂ by common denominators, before any rational-line choice. S002 uses the two M conclusions and the explicit finite-coordinate tensor isomorphism to get n=nr, hence r=1. Only then S003 chooses nonzero a and compatible rational generators. S004 proves unit factors and uses a finite minimum to establish J=Rb with b∈J, b≠0; S005 proves the R-basis. No field-containment shortcut or hidden freeness of J is used.",source_application_check:"At R004/S002 M002 is instantiated with A=ℚ, B=R, C=M_R. R⊂ℚ is a unital algebra inclusion; N002 gives the required free module, with finrank n. Strong rank condition for R is justified there by clearing denominators of a rational kernel vector and applying field dimension; for ℚ it is field dimension. The exact delivered conclusion is dim_ℚ(ℚ⊗_R M_R)=n. M001 is instantiated at the same S with A=ℚ, B=I, C_i=QJ. N001 gives finite I of size n and prior F001 gives QJ finite-dimensional, hence free and finitely generated. Its exact conclusion is the finite product dimension sum nr. The displayed coordinate isomorphism supplies the bridge equating those two vector-space dimensions. Source obligations match the complete probed signatures.",declaration_check:"QJ is defined before its finite-dimensionality is proved; r is introduced at S002 from prior F001. Witnesses a,k,g come from the nonzero finite module in N003, and q is grounded in prior F001,F002 plus those compatible choices. The exponent family eta, unit-factor candidates u, minimum ν and explicit b=p^ν a are introduced at S004 and their properties proved there; no type grants unit status. Pure-tensor variables ρ,c0,d0 and gamma are accounted for in S001–S002, with denominators only inverted when nonzero. Private a,g,q,eta,u,ν do not occur free in N004