{id:"R005",dependency_and_local_assumption_check:"H001 grounds kappa and both reductions; H002 gives all factorial index bounds. S001 writes the first two inverse maps and checks tensor relations, using N002 for lattice stability. S002 proves R/pR≅F_p by image and kernel and writes the quotient-tensor inverse maps, using p=0 in K. S003 selects b from N004 and extends its actual R-basis through coordinate maps to obtain the K-basis and reduced operator matrices. S004 descends the precise N002 E identity, and multiplies the integer divided-power identities by factorial inverses available for every index in that formula. No choice of b∈K or assumption v∈M is made.",source_application_check:"No E/M is invoked. The tensor changes of scalar rings are justified by the actual balanced maps and their inverse composites at S001–S002. Basis extension at S003 is checked by spanning pure tensors and extended coordinate functionals. The representation change from complex E_ij to K-linear T_ij uses N002's preservation of M_R, so it is a valid induced operator. Units map to units under kappa, and S004 checks all needed factorials with H001–H002.",declaration_check:"m,c,s and u are scoped to their tensor-map formulas. The nonzero generator b is chosen from N004 at S003; beta_i is then defined using the prior F001 isomorphism and N002's injective identification. T is defined only after N002 provides preservation. Arbitrary r,i,j,k are in I for S004. The output existentially binds b and the resulting basis family, and fully states T's formula and action, so no unexported private basis fact is required by R006."},
{id:"R006",dependency_and_local_assumption_check:"N005 directly supplies a basis, nonzeroness, factorial formulas and matrix-unit actions. Under L1 at S001, invariance under x,y extends to all T_ij using exactly the index window stated in N005. S002 closes the zero branch L2. S003 under L3 proves the joint existence F003 before S004 selects w,c,j. S004 uses F001 and N005 to obtain c_j beta_i∈W, divides by c_j≠0 and concludes W=V_K; L3 is discharged into F004. S005 exhausts the two cases, discharges L1 and quantifies arbitrary W. H003 justifies the spanning Lie action, and H001–H002 justify the final characteristic/range endpoint comments.",source_application_check:"No E/M is invoked. Closure of a linear subspace under scalar multiples and finite compositions is applied with N005's explicit formula, whose only inverses are proved nonzero there. The passage from T_ij w to c_j beta_i is obtained by linearity on the full basis expansion F003. Division uses the field structure on K and F003's c_j≠0. The L_K equivalence follows from the explicit spanning Chevalley lattice, with no faithfulness or algebraic-closure premise.",declaration_check:"The beta witness is provided by N005; T is its explicitly defined family of reduced operators. W is arbitrary. The witnesses w,c,j are selected compatibly from prior F003 under L3 and confined to S004, while arbitrary i ranges over I. F001 consistently binds i0,j0 in T_i0j0. F003's w0,c0,j0 bind its entire joint existence statement. F004 and P contain none of those private witnesses. All L1,L2,L3 introductions and discharges agree with the actual prose."}
